<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander Kerensky</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1881–1970</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander Kerensky was a Russian socialist lawyer who served in the Provisional Government after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/february-revolution">February Revolution</a> of 1917, first as justice and war minister and from July as its head. He proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> a republic in September 1917 and was overthrown by the Bolsheviks in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/october-revolution">October Revolution</a>. He spent the rest of his life in exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-kerensky.jpg" alt="Alexander Kerensky" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karl Bulla · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexander_Kerensky_1917_Crop.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
